# Restart drain discipline

**Invariant:** `restart(service) ⇒ drain(in_flight) ∧ (wait_background ∨ wait_inwindow)` —
never `kill(in_flight)`, and never `skip(restart)` because the service is busy.

Operator bind 2026-07-31; MCP same-window classifier 2026-08-05. Failure class:
a seat facing busy either (a) preempted **another** seat's live work with
`force=true`, or (b) abandoned the restart and left a fix landed-not-live.
Both are wrong.

**Busy is a probe signal, not a wait verdict.** Classify what the probe means
(GIW write lease vs MCP streaming vs idle/ghost CSE), then choose wait vs force.
`busy=true` / `live_cse_count>0` alone never licenses “park forever” or “skip restart.”

## CSE vs service process (BINDING — 2026-08-12)

```
identity(CSE) = chat_url
restart(mcp | cdp_ask | …) ⇒ drop(attach) ∧ ¬end(CSE)
```

A Cowork CSE is a Chrome tab. Satellite `execution_id`, Playwright, and the MCP
socket are **attach handles**. Recycling those processes is reconnect, not
session-kill. Cowork is **not tightly coupled** to mcp/cdp_ask — the tab
survives; recover after `wait_healthy`. `cdp_ask` `sync_restart` is **never
coupled to mcp** (`api_dispatch._sync_restart`). After `cdp_ask` recycle:
`wait_healthy` → `project_ask(op=followup)` / `reattach=true` by `chat_url`
(tab should still be open). Continuity hop (new window, same private lane) is
for **MCP tooling/chip refresh**, not because a satellite row died.

MCP other-window **streaming** wait still applies — that protects another seat's
in-tab tools mid-turn, not CSE lifetime. Do not narrate `running_count` /
`execution_id` gone as “the CSE is dead.” **Forbidden:** skip, park, or
withhold MCP `sync_restart` because it “would drop Cowork attach.” Attach-loss
is expected and recoverable.

## The three wrong moves

| Wrong | Why | Right |
|---|---|---|
| `force=true` to kill **another** seat's streaming / write lease | Preempts unrelated in-flight work | Wait (MCP other-window) or arm durable drain (GIW) |
| "Busy / a dispatch or CSE is running, so I won't restart" | Leaves the fix landed-not-live; treats `cdp_ask` attach-loss as session-kill | Arm the restart. After `cdp_ask`: recover the tab by `chat_url`. MCP-force only when the classifier says so |
| "MCP restart would drop Cowork attach / kill the CSE" | Conflates attach handle with CSE identity (`chat_url`) | Restart per classifier. Recover: followup/reattach or continuity hop after healthy |
| Sit in-window polling `wait_healthy` while holding a lease | The lease you hold is what the drain waits on — never converges (friction 25989) | Arm, then **exit**; probe after |

## Mechanism already exists — use it, do not reinvent

`manage(action="sync_restart"|"restart"|"stop", service=…)` is drain-gated at the
shared chokepoint (`scripts/model_manager/ui/controller/restart_drain.py`), so both
MCP agents and the TUI get the same guard. Two shapes:

| Service | Behavior on busy |
|---|---|
| `git_integration_worker` | Durable **drain supervision** — worker stops accepting new mutating work, existing dispatches run to completion, SIGTERM only after `active_count == 0`. Returns `status=deferred, state=draining` with a `restart_intent_id`. Deadline is days, not seconds: drain is assumed inevitable |
| `mcp` | Busy-probe deferral — **not** NullBusyProbe. Defers when `cdp_ask` reports live CSE / running project-ask **or** MCP `/active-work` reports in-flight HTTP or recent life `tools/call` (TTL). Container SIGTERM HTTP drain alone does **not** protect Cowork between POSTs |
| `cdp_ask` | Busy when `effective_count > 0` (`max(running, live_cse)`) — `live_cse_count` = **observed open CSE tabs** on CDP ports (`/json/list` URL match), **not** “streaming”. Product concurrency: open tabs may be many; only ≤3 may **stream** at once (`claude-ai-cdp-navigation` § Parallel Chrome) |
| everything else | Busy-probe deferral — `status=deferred, state ∈ {busy, in_progress, probe_error}` with `retry_after_s` |

Read state without touching the gate: `manage(action="busy_status")` — returns
`busy`, `restart_would_defer`, `active_work_summary` (one-line holder identity —
prefer it), and `restart_intent` per service. Safe to poll live.

## MCP / life-surface seat discipline (BINDING)

`mcp.busy=false` historically meant "no probe," not "Cowork idle." Before any
`sync_restart`/`restart`/`stop` of **mcp**, read `busy_status` (`mcp` + `cdp_ask`).
GIW code pickup does **not** require MCP restart. Descriptor / tooling MCP edits
follow the **same-window force protocol** below (operator bind 2026-08-05).

### MCP force vs wait — same-window protocol (BINDING — 2026-08-05)

**Narrow classifier (primary):** wait only when a CSE is **streaming** and belongs
to **another** window. Everything else restarts.

```
[streaming]
  same_window  ⇒ force  // after healthy: MCP tool surface dead — continuity hop advised
  other_window ⇒ wait ≺ call  // never force
[¬streaming]   ⇒ restart  // force=true if probe defers on idle/ghost live_cse
```

| Condition | Action |
|---|---|
| **¬streaming** (incl. idle CSE tabs / ghost `live_cse>0` with `running_count=0`) | Restart — `force=true` if a false busy defers |
| Streaming ∧ **this** window (same CSE / this seat's life connection) | **`force=true` OK** — expect MCP tool surface dead mid-stream; after `wait_healthy(mcp)`, **continuity hop** (new CDP window on same private lane) — ¬ warm follow-up alone for tooling refresh |
| Streaming ∧ **another** window | **Wait** → then call (no force) |

`live_cse_count` ≠ streaming. Observed CSE pages without an active stream are
idle/ghost — **¬** other-window wait. Open-tab count may be arbitrary; the
streaming concurrency bound (≤3 simultaneous; >3 untested) lives in
`claude-ai-cdp-navigation` — this rule only classifies restart force vs wait.

**Same-window force** covers IDE lead and operator-proxy (`cdp/opus` / web-anthropic
on `purpose=operator-proxy|mission`) when the busy reason is **this** seat's
`cdp_ask_live` / MCP session. Operator-proxy often exercises via `contract: propagate`
(cursor-auto may auto-apply self-preempt force when `allow_self_preempt` is true).
¬ GIW force under this protocol. ¬ force to clear **another** window's stream.

Tooling / descriptor restart sequence after same-window force: restart →
**wait mcp healthy** → **continuity hop** (`cdp-operator-proxy` Refresh ≠ follow-up).
Commissioning continuity **before** healthy is a defect.

Anti-patterns:
- treat `mcp.busy=false` + `in_flight=0` as proof Cowork life is idle
- treat `live_cse_count>0` / `busy=true` as automatic wait (missing the streaming test)
- treat ghost/idle `live_cse` as "other window"
- skip MCP/`cdp_ask` restart to “protect Cowork”; narrate `drop(attach)` as ending the CSE

## Procedure (binding)

1. **Probe before deciding** — `manage(action="busy_status")`. For **mcp** /
   **cdp_ask**, run the streaming/window classifier above; for **GIW**, `busy`
   means arm durable drain (¬ force).
2. **Fire the restart anyway.** Deferral is success when the classifier says wait
   (other-window stream / GIW drain). When the classifier says ¬streaming or
   same-window stream, `force=true` clears false busy — do not park on `live_cse`.
3. **Then wait, per seat:**
   - **Holding a write lease** (cursor-sdk / `cursor_sdk_gate`, or the dispatch
     whose work the drain is waiting on): the envelope's
     `caller_must_exit_to_release_lease` is binding — **exit now**, do not
     `wait_healthy` in-window. Your own exit is what lets the drain converge.
   - **IDE lead:** wait in the **background** (`presence-discipline` P4) — do not
     pin the turn. Poll `busy_status` / `wait_healthy` on a later turn, or let the
     `git_worker.drain.*` events land.
   - **cursor-auto:** report the armed `restart_intent_id` on the CLOSEOUT and
     finish. Do not block the dispatch on someone else's drain.
4. **Verify live before claiming live.** Landed ≠ live. Confirm the restart
   completed (process start time after the commit, or a live probe of the changed
   surface) before any claim that a fix is in effect.

## `force=true` — narrow

Permitted when **any**:

- the human operator explicitly authorizes preempting in-flight work, **or**
- the in-flight work is provably this seat's own and abandonable, **or**
- **MCP same-window protocol** (above): ¬streaming / ghost `live_cse` false busy,
  **or** this seat's streaming CSE — force (+ continuity after healthy when the
  stream was this window); **other-window stream** ⇒ wait, never force

Never as a reaction to latency alone, and never to make an unrelated seat's
deferral go away. ¬ `force=true` on `git_integration_worker` under the MCP
same-window protocol.

Killing a bridge or worker process directly (`pkill`, `kill`, `docker stop`) is
forbidden for lifecycle — `services_ws.mdc` § Scripts.

